```c
header = MHD_lookup_connection_value(connection, MHD_HEADER_KIND, "Content-Length");
if (!header)
    return mhd_respond(connection, MHD_HTTP_LENGTH_REQUIRED,
                       "Content-Length header is required.");
```
Reason:
The code incorrectly requires the `Content-Length` header even when the `Transfer-Encoding` is set to `chunked`. In chunked transfers, the `Content-Length` header should not be specified, leading to potential HTTP protocol violations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
header = MHD_lookup_connection_value(connection, MHD_HEADER_KIND, "Transfer-Encoding");
if (header) {
    if (!strcaseeq(header, "chunked"))
        return mhd_respondf(connection, 0, MHD_HTTP_BAD_REQUEST,
                            "Unsupported Transfer-Encoding type: %s", header);
    chunked = true;
}
if (header) {
    if (chunked)
        return mhd_respond(connection, MHD_HTTP_BAD_REQUEST,
                           "Content-Length must not specified when Transfer-Encoding type is 'chunked'");
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check for the `Transfer-Encoding` header to determine if it is set to `chunked`. If it is, the code correctly prevents the requirement for the `Content-Length` header, thus adhering to HTTP protocol standards and avoiding the previous oversight.

